course: dictionary
lesson: 4107
title: The giver
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A giver is a person who gives. The ending -er often means someone who does something: a writer writes, a teacher teaches, a giver gives. «Saying thank you soon tells the giver it arrived safely and that you liked it.» Here the giver is the person who gave you the present.
explain: Look at the words around giver to check its meaning. «For birthday or holiday presents, write a short thank-you note or card to each giver within a week or two.» Each giver is a person who has given you something, so that is who the note goes to.
explain: Giver can also describe a kind person who likes to give. A cheerful giver gives with a happy heart, and a generous giver shares freely. «Keeping quiet and acting surprised lets the giver enjoy the moment.» Here the giver is the one who enjoys giving the surprise.
fact: A giver is a person who gives something to others, such as a present, money, time or help.
fact: A giver can also be a kind, generous person who likes to give.
fact: The plural of giver is givers.
fact: Blood givers, also called donors, give blood to help people in hospital.
fact: In «A girl in Vancouver gets the same book from two aunts», the two aunts are the givers.
exercise: «Saying thank you soon tells the giver it arrived safely.» Who is the giver here? | *The person who gave the present | The parcel | The shop that sold it | The postman who delivered it
exercise: Which phrase describes a kind person who likes to give? | a broken clock | *a cheerful giver | a closed door | a slow runner
exercise: What is another name for a blood giver? | a patient | a surgeon | a nurse | *a donor
test: «A girl gets the same book from two aunts.» How many givers are there in this sentence? | None | One | *Two | Three
test: What is the plural of giver? | giveers | *givers | gives | givens
exam: Which of these means a kind person who likes to give? | a taker | a lost parcel | *a generous giver | a thank-you note
